{"id": "EUVD-2026-105091", "enisaUuid": "7bc3d320-998f-3e6c-a757-84dc1c4c7e2a", "description": "FlexGet before 3.20.7 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the decompress plugin that allows remote attackers to write arbitrary files by supplying malicious archive member paths. Attackers can deliver zip or rar archives with ../ sequences or absolute paths through a feed, writing Python files into the plugins directory for code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:54:14", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Flexget/Flexget/security/advisories/GHSA-6v57-v478-59v9", "https://github.com/Flexget/Flexget/commit/38fa748461e20befee942f5c79d8a098edea5c1f", "https://github.com/Flexget/Flexget/releases/tag/v3.20.7", "https://github.com/Flexget/Flexget/blob/v3.20.6/flexget/components/archives/decompress.py#L74-L77", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/flexget-before-3.20.7-path-traversal-zip-slip-via-decompress-plugin"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h98p-724m-phfr", "CVE-2026-113613"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.77, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c42faecb-3ac2-3cc4-a9ac-79719ff313ac", "product": {"name": "FlexGet", "vendor": {"name": "FlexGet"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.20.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "15e1e7b1-8b5d-398c-96a5-83091680a3d4", "vendor": {"name": "FlexGet"}}], "isExploited": false}